  "body_html": "<h2>Two apps, two audiences</h2>\n<p>Reading Tracker is a hobby project for my own reading. I read in English and Vietnamese, mostly paper books, and wanted three answers: how much I really read, at what pace, and when I will finish the current book. The tracker is for me: a private Streamlit app on localhost only. One big Start and one big Stop button log a session, with the page where I stopped already filled in<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<p>The dashboard is for visitors, with a finish-date range for the current book. It is live, but on a seeded demo history of 15 books and 180 sessions over 182 days, labelled \"Demo data\", because my real history is not imported yet. It is a hobby, but it covers the whole path of a data product, from a written spec to a live deployment<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<h2>Design decisions</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Friction decides the data.</strong> The spec's first goal is logging a session in under 10 seconds, because friction kills the habit and the data. So two big buttons come first, and everything else hides in expanders. It is a target; I have not timed it<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</li>\n<li><strong>Private by construction.</strong> The export drops notes and end times, floors start times to the hour and keeps each duration in whole seconds. Rounding both ends would turn a 20:10 to 20:40 session into 20:00 to 20:00: zero minutes. This way pace survives, and the clock shows only the hour<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</li>\n<li><strong>Raw events, checked at the door.</strong> SQLite stores only books and sessions, and rules refuse bad rows before saving. Everything else is derived in pandas, so a fixed rule changes every past number consistently<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</li>\n<li><strong>A baseline before a model.</strong> The finish date is two plain ratios over the last 28 days, with nothing learned. It has no accuracy figure yet: measuring one needs my real history and a backtest<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</li>\n<li><strong>One brand, defined once.</strong> The palette and fonts live in <code>brand.py</code>, mirrored in the Streamlit theme, and a test forbids hex codes anywhere else. Since v1.1.0 the dashboard wears my site's Regent brand, matching the page that embeds it<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Under the hood</h2>\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-title\">The privacy export is the only path from my private log to the public dashboard</div><div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"stage\" style=\"flex-grow:1\"><div class=\"stage-label\">1 · Capture</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Private tracker</div><div class=\"box-detail\">For me: one big Start and one big Stop button</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Streamlit, localhost only</li><li>Last page prefilled</li><li>Live timer</li><li>Past sessions and books in expanders</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ one reading session</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage\" style=\"flex-grow:1\"><div class=\"stage-label\">2 · Check and store</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Rules, then SQLite</div><div class=\"box-detail\">A bad row is refused before it is saved</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>One active session at a time</li><li>No overlapping or future sessions</li><li>Positions within the book</li><li>ISO 8601 times with UTC offset</li><li>Text in Unicode NFC</li><li>No ORM</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ books + sessions, raw events only</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage stage--parallel\" style=\"flex-grow:1.6\"><div class=\"stage-label\">3 · Publish</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Privacy export</div><div class=\"box-detail\">My real data, minus what is private</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Notes and end times dropped</li><li>Start times floored to the hour</li><li>Duration kept in whole seconds</li><li>Active sessions left out</li></ul></div><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Demo history</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Synthetic, through the same validation</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Seed 10, 182 days</li><li>15 books, 180 sessions</li><li>English and Vietnamese</li><li>Labelled “Demo data”</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ public tables</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage stage--parallel\" style=\"flex-grow:1.6\"><div class=\"stage-label\">4 · Derive</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Reading features</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Pure pandas functions, nothing stored</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Duration, pages, pages per minute</li><li>Daily minutes, current and longest streak</li><li>A session over midnight counts for its start date</li><li>Audiobooks count for minutes, not page pace</li></ul></div><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Finish estimate</div><div class=\"box-detail\">A baseline: two plain ratios, nothing learned</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Pages left ÷ median pace ÷ minutes per day</li><li>Window: the last 28 days</li><li>Range from 25th and 75th percentile pace</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ pace, streaks, finish range</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage stage--out\" style=\"flex-grow:1\"><div class=\"stage-label\">5 · Show</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Public dashboard</div><div class=\"box-detail\">For visitors: Streamlit and Plotly, in the site&#x27;s brand</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Current book and finish range</li><li>Calendar heatmap and streaks</li><li>Weekly minutes against a goal</li><li>Pace by genre, format, language</li><li>Timeline of finished and abandoned books</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ live on Streamlit Community Cloud</div></div></div><figcaption>Stages 1 and 2 run on my computer only. Stage 3 publishes my real data minus what is private, or a synthetic demo history. Until my history is imported, the live dashboard shows the demo.</figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>The stack is small on purpose: my spec ruled out an ORM, a web framework and Docker. Text is stored in Unicode NFC, so Vietnamese diacritics typed on different keyboards group together. The demo history goes through the same validation as real data, so both sources on the public side pass the same rules<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<h2>Built, tested and shipped</h2>\n<p>I started with the spec, not the code. The repo's first commit is its <code>CLAUDE.md</code>, with my goals, the stack limits, the data model and the privacy rules, plus the brand guide. Then I built the product with Claude Code, which co-authored every commit, and released v1.0.0 the same day, after 29 commits<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-title\">The data rules have full coverage; the Windows launcher is the weak spot</div><div class=\"dotplot\"><div class=\"dp-legend\"><i></i>All code 94.75</div><div class=\"dp-row dp-row--axis\"><div class=\"dp-label dp-axis-title\">Line coverage, % (higher is better)</div><div class=\"dp-track dp-axis\"><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:0.00%\">40.0</span><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:33.33%\">60.0</span><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:66.67%\">80.0</span><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:100.00%\">100.0</span></div><div></div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Private tracker</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">app/tracker.py · 22 click-through tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:94.52%\" title=\"Private tracker: 96.71\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">96.71</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Data rules</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">log.py · 109 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:100.00%\" title=\"Data rules: 100.00\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">100.00</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Storage</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">db.py · 24 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:100.00%\" title=\"Storage: 100.00\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">100.00</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Privacy export</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">export.py · 11 tests, shared with the demo</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:90.20%\" title=\"Privacy export: 94.12\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">94.12</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Demo history</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">synthetic.py · the same 11 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:98.37%\" title=\"Demo history: 99.02\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">99.02</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Reading features</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">features.py · 19 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:100.00%\" title=\"Reading features: 100.00\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">100.00</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Finish estimate</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">eta.py · 6 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:91.87%\" title=\"Finish estimate: 95.12\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">95.12</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Public dashboard</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">app/dashboard.py · 7 click-through tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:91.50%\" title=\"Public dashboard: 94.90\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">94.90</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Brand</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">brand.py · 7 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:100.00%\" title=\"Brand: 100.00\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">100.00</div></div><div class=\"dp-row dp-row--hot\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Windows launcher</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">app/launcher.py · 4 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:16.67%\" title=\"Windows launcher: 50.00\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">50.00</div></div></div><figcaption>Line coverage is the share of a part&#x27;s statements that the tests run, measured with pytest-cov on v1.1.1; it is not part of CI. Rows follow the pipeline, then the shared parts. The dashed line is all code, 849 of 896 statements. The launcher&#x27;s untested half starts the server in the background, waits for it and opens the browser.</figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>On v1.1.1, 209 tests pass, and GitHub Actions runs them with ruff on every push. Click-through tests with Streamlit AppTest drive both apps. Each of the 3 releases is tagged and passed CI: v1.0.0, then v1.1.0 in the site's brand, then v1.1.1, whose charts no longer zoom on a drag or swipe. The dashboard has been live on Streamlit Community Cloud since 2026-10-25; this page shows a still of it and loads the live app only when you ask<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<h2>Roadmap</h2>\n<p>Importing my reading history from Toggl comes first; until then, the dashboard stays on demo data. Then comes the spec's third goal: a Bayesian time-to-finish model with a backtest, which I will mostly write myself. That backtest is also what the baseline needs before its accuracy can be measured<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<h2>Tools</h2>\n<p>Python, uv, SQLite, pandas, Streamlit, Plotly, pytest, ruff, GitHub Actions, Claude Code.</p>\n<h2>Links</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Live dashboard, on demo data: <a href=\"https://tung-anh-reading.streamlit.app\">https://tung-anh-reading.streamlit.app</a></li>\n<li>Code repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/feitandodatascience/reading-tracker\">https://github.com/feitandodatascience/reading-tracker</a></li>\n</ul>",
